//! `extern "C"` command wrappers over `marmot_uniffi::Marmot`.
//!
//! Every wrapper follows the same shape, so almost all of them are
//! generated by [`c_cmd!`]:
//!
//! - `ffi_guard` around the body (no unwinding into C).
//! - Borrowed inputs read with `required_str` / `optional_str` /
//!   `str_array` / input-struct `to_ffi`; caller memory is never freed.
//! - Async runtime methods run via `client.block_on`.
//! - Results convert to `#[repr(C)]` mirrors, move to the heap, and are
//!   written through the out-pointer; the caller releases them with the
//!   type's `marmot_*_free`.
//! - Errors map through `status::status_from_error`.
//!
//! Commands with struct/byte inputs are written by hand below the macro
//! block.

